# Routes and controllers

Express service under `src/` only.

## Routes

Order on every protected route: `auth(...rights)` → `validate(schema)` → controller.

Register the module in `src/routes/v1/index.js` and mount it under `/v1`.

```javascript
router
  .route('/admin')
  .post(auth('create-employees'), validate(userValidation.createUser), userController.createUser)
  .get(auth('read-employees'), validate(userValidation.getUsers), userController.getUsers);

router.post('/login', validate(authValidation.login), authController.login);
```

Do not put the controller before auth or validate. Do not skip `validate`.

Rights come from `req.accessList` (parsed from the `x-access-list` header in `app.js`). Do not trust the client role alone. Only the gateway may set that header. Strip a client-supplied `x-access-list` on any request that did not come from the gateway. A browser or public caller cannot grant itself rights by sending the header.

## Controllers

- Wrap every async handler with `catchAsync`.
- Throw `ApiError` for expected failures.
- Respond with `model.transform()`. Never send a raw doc that includes a password.
- Use `httpStatus` constants, not magic numbers.
- Use `getQueryOptions(req.query)` for pagination and sort.
- Use `pick` for allowlisted query and body fields.
- Keep the controller thin. A simple DB check can stay. Heavy logic goes to a service or helper.

```javascript
const createUser = catchAsync(async (req, res) => {
  if (await User.isMobileTaken(req.body.mobile)) {
    throw new ApiError(httpStatus.BAD_REQUEST, 'Mobile already taken');
  }
  const employeeId = await generateEmployeeId();
  const password = generatedPassword();
  const user = await User.create({ ...req.body, employeeId, password, createdBy: req.user._id });
  res.status(httpStatus.CREATED).send(user.transform());
});

const getUsers = catchAsync(async (req, res) => {
  const filter = pick(req.query, ['name', 'role_id', 'store_id']);
  const options = getQueryOptions(req.query);
  const [users, total] = await Promise.all([
    User.find(filter, null, options).populate('createdBy', 'name email mobile'),
    User.countDocuments(filter),
  ]);
  res.send({
    data: users.map((u) => u.transform()),
    pagination: {
      total,
      page: options.skip / options.limit + 1,
      totalPages: Math.ceil(total / options.limit),
    },
  });
});
```

Do not hand-write try/catch and `res.status(500)`, and do not `res.send(user)` on a raw document. A missing record throws `ApiError` `NOT_FOUND`. `User.create(req.body)` and `User.find(req.body)` are not allowed. The route is validated first, then business checks run, and filters use `pick`.
